note bottom of LIB
  The smoke calls Burn in process so its
  fixed model needs no scoring subprocess.
  Native baseline selectors consume composed
  queues without presenting synthetic weights
  as fitted parameters or a learned policy.
end note

note bottom of CONTRACTS
  Full canonical keys preserve action order
  and prevent digest collisions from merging
  distinct candidates. Native helpers supply
  rules and costs while Rust owns composition,
  resource accounting and mine reservations.
end note

note bottom of COMPOSER
  Queue each valid child before an owner,
  duplicate or quota skip can discard it.
  Later extensions may qualify for retention
  even when their parent cannot obtain
  capacity from the current funding lane.
end note

note bottom of PLANNER
  Planning derives knowledge from authorized
  cells and own facts, never private snapshots.
  Count mine entities rather than distinct
  squares so duplicate locations still consume
  the native three-mine capacity.
end note

note bottom of MODEL
  Set the dtype before creating tensors, because
  widening rounded values cannot restore lost
  bits. Zero padding gives the proof its fixed
  input shape without implementing the economic
  feature encoder.
end note

note bottom of PACK
  Use Burnpack for checkpoint fixtures so JSON
  cannot substitute for the backend serializer.
  Restoring must preserve each parameter bit
  and reject corrupt data without admitting a
  learned model.
end note

note bottom of XTASK
  Previous receipts describe a narrower runtime
  and cannot authorize the new delivery.
  Every required result must bind to unchanged
  source before any reviewer may participate.
end note

note bottom of LEDGER_CONTRACTS
  Node imports economic tables from native
  rules so Rust cannot fork their authority.
  Closed boundary checks validate inputs, but
  only the host can bind their provenance
  to a recorded native run.
end note

note bottom of LEDGER_HISTORY
  Resolve each subject against the group's
  immutable preimage and accepted births.
  Stage all effects before checking geometry,
  so swaps and same-cell replacements retain
  their native identity and paid lineage.
end note

note bottom of LEDGER_WORK
  Both seats share one meter within a window,
  so helper calls cannot renew its allowance.
  Failed updates preserve ledger state without
  refunding charges or certifying runtime
  capacity for the deferred feature encoder.
end note

legend bottom
  Baseline proof remains historical in native-runner.md; ledger proof lives in native-economic-ledger.md.
  Preserve exact B funding: seven lanes x 48 + shared 175 + pass.
  All lanes enumerate full domains; only availability probes filter families.
  Preserve counters, continuation-before-skip and capacity/attempt/exhausted precedence.
  Retained Burn 0.22.0 Flex CPU f64 smoke/checkpoint fixtures are synthetic only.
  Width 418 remains zero padding, not the R4 feature encoder.
  Native baselines use no learned scorer; learned=false / modelArtifact=null.
  Native tables: turns 1-10 mineral/gas 1/1; 11-20 2/2; 21-45 3/3.
  Initial endowment is not a grant; only settlement advances grantOrdinal.
  Own bank = origin + actual credits - paid debits; capped credit may be zero.
  Paid debits = surviving + destroyed + wasted basis; promotion preserves basis.
  CC lives stay separate; ordinary king replacement=0, native unit cost=1.
  Mines remain entities, not a Set; memory does not identify unique enemy population.
  Keep only the last pair's full canonical bytes; older duplicate ordinals refuse.
  Birth mode / transform toMode: required tank|siege for rook, explicit null otherwise.
  Native origin modes only; no predecessor inference, Tank default or compatibility parser.
  F1 input is a standalone checked library, not a CLI/live-policy/native-permit integration.
  lib.rs exports feature_input and feature_manifest; no retained scorer calls either module.
  Replay preserves latest innovations/grant; Y2 counts each witness FACT ENTRY, not group keys.
  History owns crate-private seed types; sorted detached units and stable mine IDs leave state intact.
  Metadata 418 = queue34 + 4xposition84 + economic12 + promotion36; no feature values/masks/formulas.
  Manifest S=25864; build=452544; successful validation=119344; existing ledger fees remain additional.
  F2 constants: learning rate .001 / temperature 1 / L2 .0001; zero418 weights / no bias.
  F2 production is scalar Rust; ONLY its tests use Burn, not a production math backend.
  Math EpisodeStatistics is not a native eligible episode; SgdProposal is not weight-update permission.
  No math-to-game/CLI/native-permit/feature-encoder/geometry/checkpoint/baseline-commit runtime edge.
  Every product/add/subtraction is finite-checked; F2 does not reuse compat abs(value)<=1e6.
  No new meter/allowance or whole-decision resource claim; O(512+418) buffers are not admission.
  F3 point input/grant/rows are hypothetical DATA, not native-adapter or fitted-table permission.
  Z/N/Den are unconditioned; L/destination retain raw mass, never a normalized posterior.
  Boolean point support has no counts/model-zero dependence and is not complete publicSupport.
  Storage 8034 headstock / 7501 joint / 5x33 Gamma / 8192 rows; reachable J<=609, not617.
  Physical max input may BUDGET-refuse; same caller work retains spent charges, no partial result.
  No kernel-to-host/native-permit/cohort/likelihood/spatial-envelope/collector/calibration runtime edge.
  Verifier notEstablished: full-training-closure / genuine-native-authority / whole-decision-adequacy.
  Verifier notEstablished also includes calibration / training-readiness; private labels remain DOCUMENT ONLY.
  No real training, payout calibration, R4 readiness or activation claim.
  Complete fresh static/functional/preservation/diagram/source-identity gates precede reviewers.
